+ * loop waits for its vblank count exactly that way (lock 0x7B8BC0, wait
+ * 0x7B8CD8, unlock 0x7B8BF8; its vblank handler signals through 0x7B9138), so
+ * at 60 ticks every frame lost one or two Windows sleep quanta (~1-4 ms of
+ * 16.7). Now a signal (any lwcond) bumps a sequence and wakes every waiter; a
+ * wait returns at once if the sequence moved since this thread's last wait --
+ * a signal delivered meanwhile, also by the gcm pump at this very HLE call --
+ * and otherwise sleeps until a signal, at most the old 1 ms. Every return is
+ * still a possible spurious wakeup the guest loop re-checks, as before. The
+ * vblank beat calls ppu_lwcond_wake_all so a waiter runs the vblank handler at
+ * once. PS3_LWCOND_POLL=1 = the old fixed sleep. */
